  "id" : "1D8BD95B-B724-4028-A124-D3C17908094A",
  "notes" : [
    {
      "note" : "# Local Vision Language Model\n\nA Vision language Model (VLM) is a large language model that understands images or sequences of images. \n\nThis node lets you chose from a selection of VLM’s available to run locally. Node some of these require a LOT of Ram and disk space, and might not be actually able to run on all systems. \n\nWhen you chose a VLM, it will download from Hugging Face and then execute as long as the “Generate” toggle is set to true.\n\nSome VLMs can do instruction following, so experiment with a prompt!\n\nYou can ask them to describe the contents of the image, or whatever you want.\n",
      "id" : "A5D08476-7947-4CBF-B4D0-E6522FB6031B",
      "rect" : [
        [
          -998.5,
          -314
        ],
        [
          500,
          500
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
